1. **MEDIUM | [RecordingArchive.kt:28](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/keep-recordings/app/src/main/java/com/envi/wispr/ui/RecordingArchive.kt:28).** If `getExternalFilesDir()` returns null, `keep` returns silently. That contradicts the revised G1 promise that a warning names why a recording was not kept ([plan:41](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/keep-recordings/docs/feature-requests/issue-373-2026-09-25-keep-recordings.md:41)). **Fix:** throw `NotKept("recordings storage unavailable")`; change the null-folder test to expect it, and test that `CapturedAudioFiles` logs that reason while continuing cleanup.

2. **MEDIUM | [RecordingArchive.kt:33](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/keep-recordings/app/src/main/java/com/envi/wispr/ui/RecordingArchive.kt:33), [RecordingArchive.kt:48](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/keep-recordings/app/src/main/java/com/envi/wispr/ui/RecordingArchive.kt:48).** A failed stale-part deletion does not stop the copy. After the new WAV is saved, `keep` throws and the caller warns that it was not kept. If the source is also missing, the source warning masks the cleanup failure. The `finally` block also ignores failure to delete the current `.part` ([RecordingArchive.kt:46](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/keep-recordings/app/src/main/java/com/envi/wispr/ui/RecordingArchive.kt:46)). **Fix:** report failed stale-part cleanup before writing; report a failed current-part deletion without describing a successfully published WAV as missing. Add tests for both cleanup failures.

